<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Abubakar Tafawa Balewa</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1912–1966</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Abubakar Tafawa Balewa was a Nigerian politician of the Northern People's Congress who became federal prime minister in 1957 and led <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nigeria">Nigeria</a> to independence on 1 October 1960. He remained prime minister of the independent federation until he was killed in the military coup of January 1966.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/abubakar-tafawa-balewa.jpg" alt="Abubakar Tafawa Balewa" width="320" height="479" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Eliot Elisofon · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Tafawa_Balewa_in_office_02.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
